cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lausanne: a local, confidentiality-preserving creativity support tool for legal documentation"
message: "If you use this software or its design principles, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumawat
    given-names: Aaditya
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Technology Delhi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AadityaK21/lausanne"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - legal-ai
  - speech-recognition
  - speaker-diarization
  - summarization
  - hallucination
  - design-science-research
  - privacy-preserving-ml
abstract: >-
  A fully local pipeline that converts legal proceeding audio into
  speaker-attributed, citation-backed notes, together with an evaluation
  harness measuring word error rate on legally load-bearing tokens,
  diarization error rate, and note faithfulness. Introduces model-selected
  extraction, in which a language model's response schema is restricted to
  source identifiers so that fabricated content is structurally inexpressible
  rather than merely improbable.
